\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $2$ pivots in the $2$nd and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $1$st column."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1721f54d-1a88-5c12-bbde-d1d984fe2e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263218} {:answer/id #uuid "27e585a7-a606-505f-be05-1ea25cef0a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263346} {:answer/id #uuid "7961919d-a389-5542-83bc-46af803018d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264053} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6df512-73a0-5675-a4f5-53e233594c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264781} {:answer/id #uuid "db26d949-a948-56f0-973e-1f526ba19e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb6df512-73a0-5675-a4f5-53e233594c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264781} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ffe2d2-a7bc-51b0-b9cd-9f64b57b349a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa0e8a0d-dec0-575e-8d45-de71528bdbeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130949" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -7 & 9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -7 & 9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4148689f-f457-575d-aecc-fedd10bed85a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263580} {:answer/id #uuid "5f435920-ec0e-5fc7-a2e2-e0dcc7810666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263824} {:answer/id #uuid "9b970a7b-87ff-5a3e-94cc-812331684b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264331} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a5d22f-542b-5edf-b6c1-0a789f381be1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264541} {:answer/id #uuid "e