fore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd column."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d67e28c-a256-5a1d-9e04-f477d00894a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339387} {:answer/id #uuid "260f4b80-53d9-5f26-b97b-2b2e97e88497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd, $4$th, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339456} {:answer/id #uuid "2def53e1-c883-56b0-9c46-4ebe4d3dbc36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339534} {:answer/id #uuid "6092a204-0ea0-56e8-9213-ebd6bcdfacc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339988} {:answer/id #uuid "d76a0d0f-e606-54f1-91c8-3c6c587ad587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d76a0d0f-e606-54f1-91c8-3c6c587ad587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341037} :answer-field/id #uuid "72bbb48e-fe4e-545a-9b68-754256645b24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5f1860a-14f7-5dde-8785-3643838d3e4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73620" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $3$rd and $5$th columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124479 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "284ded16-4e2b-58c5-a9b3-3bc9411901be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339480} {:answer/id #uuid "790fe37d-c34e-5966-9eaf-9d268a97cd85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340207} {:answer/id #uuid "932e6098-7ea1-500c-a775-216015f34edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340451} {:answer/id #uuid "99f98270-ecaf-5d2c-8a85-811cc5dd4758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340515} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f3f51e-ce59-5013-95f2-552286e3b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "932e6098-7ea1-500c-a775-216015f34edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340451} :answer-field/id #uuid "362a3e08-f85f-51f6-a3a7-d6f4324787e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "949042b7-80c8-5584-b86a-21848d3ca6ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-73625" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342040 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124479 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c6719d4-8ae8-5e75-9238-9d06796f45e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339372} {:answer/id #uuid "8d95f092-36bd-5290-9f94-de1b9541f124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340400} {:answer/id #uuid "a09d0421-f482-5519-a333-aef22f6874a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ide