f the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $1$st column."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9f7d878-00f4-542b-8edf-3af17fe0109d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400550} {:answer/id #uuid "72d87fbc-4b88-5bc5-9012-5cf5dcb8fa96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400551} {:answer/id #uuid "07fc175c-99d2-576d-bf97-0bf7ed21babe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400552} {:answer/id #uuid "8987d718-6753-5003-aba1-920a4bda3fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400553} {:answer/id #uuid "99bc6b73-3d0e-57d4-97fb-808b0c314e7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9f7d878-00f4-542b-8edf-3af17fe0109d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400550} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f56b5f1-cd7e-5c89-a46d-d954a6720fb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cff88abe-cb9f-5f2b-aa6a-898f213ad5e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130955" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 9 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 9 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35bc5be3-2fe5-58fc-b85a-64fce1c7784d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400592} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee4be77-eda8-5477-a3be-58be37102e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400593} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4d6b54-8a7a-519d-b637-e37bde3dbb2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400594} {:answer/id #uuid "df41476c-0271-5fb9-ba37-452038f9f479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400595} {:answer/id #uuid "643510db-e574-5619-acbb-62a64f7e0730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "643510db-e574-5619-acbb-62a64f7e0730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400596} :answer-field/id #uuid "e34b1c74-ee10-528c-9c1b-188a96803527" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "190c1f09-7ea5-53d8-a079-57d65ed02079" :question/math-academy-id "q-131302" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aa5aa0d-c161-5543-b5f2-b208ce74003f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402450} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6786f0-4aa2-5b97-bd6a-0f94b037be70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} 