$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403661 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124477 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50e1027b-7acb-51f2-acfa-7f635f2c3e05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403663} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a71a14-cbd2-522b-997b-fd450972744e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403664} {:answer/id #uuid "5c7527ea-3828-5e2d-bf88-c0fe30aaa76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403665} {:answer/id #uuid "fdea791f-9fdb-55f9-aceb-2d7e1234420c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403666} {:answer/id #uuid "186dbf5e-ae6b-51d6-bcec-ca5ddbec9d8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c7527ea-3828-5e2d-bf88-c0fe30aaa76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403665} :answer-field/id #uuid "89c5cdb3-5a82-57f9-a194-5bfb67b87